 th a quartic interaction in $d = 4 - \\epsilon$ dimensions\, is the textbo
 ok example of a weakly coupled CFT. The epsilon expansion accurately repro
 duces the critical exponents of the $d = 3$ and the $d = 2$ Ising model. T
 his has led to the common view that WF defines a continuous family of CFTs
