SUMMARY:On “Siegel Domains” in p-adic Period Spaces
DESCRIPTION:Séminaire de géométrie arithmétique A Siegel domain is a fi
 nite-volume subset of a symmetric space whose translates under the action 
 of the relevant arithmetic group cover the entire space. In this talk\, we
  consider an analogue for the p-adic period spaces introduced by Rapoport 
 and Zink. We give a partial criterion for the existence of a Siegel domain
  and discuss its expected applications. ======\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.f
 r/event/17331/
LOCATION:IHES
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17331/
